D054 item 9 (founder, 2026-10-14; amends D039 C10, which had kept the Report-Only policy identical through launch;
task 6.6 item 3; wiki/site/tracking-inventory.md §14a): three changes to the Report-Only policy, nothing else.
  - `upgrade-insecure-requests` is dropped: a report-only policy ignores it and the browser logs an error for it on
    every page (M1's LP-tags Lighthouse runs, lighthouse-reports/2026-10-13, local only, D039).
  - connect-src admits GA4's collect host `https://www.google.com` (gtag posted its hits to www.google.com/g/collect
    as a fetch in M1's tag runs, measurement ID G-7LMKSFEXZ9 unchanged) and the Meta pixel's OpenBridge gateway,
    `https://dv-c3e594c6d429469e90b54478358619c3.ecs.us-east-1.on.aws` and its fallback
    `https://bded8a3c6ae-1-1053047382554.us-central1.run.app` (named by the pixel's own configuration,
    connect.facebook.net/signals/config/1051265191046395, read 2026-10-13; pixel ID unchanged). Both were fetches,
    so connect-src is the one directive that takes them; each is an exact origin, no wildcard.
  - The phase stays "report" (`CSP_PHASE`): the header is still Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only, so nothing that
    loads today is blocked. Every other directive, source and header is the tag's. No tracking ID, event name or
    parameter changes.

